---
source: crates/splot-cli/tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: "help(\"encode\")"
---
Encode a Y4M file to an AV2 IVF stream

Usage: splot encode [OPTIONS] --output <OUTPUT> <INPUT>

Arguments:
  <INPUT>  Input Y4M file, or `-` for standard input

Options:
  -o, --output <OUTPUT>           Output IVF file
  -v, --verbose...                Increase logging verbosity (repeatable: -v, -vv, -vvv)
      --qp <QP>                   Constant quantizer (`base_q_idx`): 1..=255 at 8 bits, 1..=303 at 10 bits; the default mode, at 80
      --quiet                     Silence all logging except errors
      --crf <CRF>                 Constant quality with lookahead offsets: rate factor 1..=63, higher is smaller
      --bitrate <BITRATE>         Target bitrate in kilobits per second
      --rc <RC>                   Bitrate mode for `--bitrate`: `vbr` (default) or `cbr` (one-second buffer) [possible values: vbr, cbr]
      --preset <PRESET>           Speed preset: 0 is the slowest and best, 10 the fastest [default: 6]
      --preset-set <FIELD=VALUE>  Overrides one field of the preset, as FIELD=VALUE; repeat for more fields. It wins over the screen-content switch. Flags take 0, 1, false or true, `tcq` takes Off, Base or All, `mvd_tools` takes three comma-separated flags. An unknown FIELD lists the valid names
      --low-delay                 Low delay: one packet per input frame, in display order. Sets `mini_gop_size=1` (IPPP, every frame shown) and `lookahead_frames=1` before `--preset-set`; off by default
      --threads <THREADS>         Worker-thread policy: `auto` (default), a positive integer, or `0` (alias for auto) [default: auto]
      --tiles <TILES>             Tile columns x rows, each a power of two up to 64. More tiles code faster on more threads and cost some compression [default: 1x1]
      --limit <LIMIT>             Stop after this many input frames
      --resize-denominator <D>    Fixed-ratio resize: codes every frame at 8/D of the input size per axis, D in 9..=16; off by default. The IVF, its decode and the `--stats` PSNR (against the resized source) are at the coded size
      --keyint <KEYINT>           Distance between key frames, in frames [default: 120]
      --stats                     Print `frame,pts,qp,bits,psnr_y,psnr_u,psnr_v` CSV lines to stdout
  -h, --help                      Print help
  -V, --version                   Print version
